  windowTitle: Microphone Setup.exe
  pageHeaders:
  - 'Step 1 of 3: Stay quiet'
  - 'Step 2 of 3: Speak normally'
  - 'Step 3 of 3: Speak loudly'
  - 'Finished: Try it out'
  quietInstruction: Stay quiet for a few seconds while we listen to your room.
  normalInstruction: Say the phrase in your normal speaking voice.
  loudInstruction: Now say it LOUDLY, like you really want to be heard.
  testInstruction: Whisper, speak normally and shout. The meter should read LOW,
    NORMAL and LOUD. Go back if it looks wrong.
  keyHintFormat: 'Hold the key and say: "{0}"'
  listeningFeedback: Listening...
  quietDoneFeedback: Captured. Click Next to continue.
  capturedFeedback: Captured.
  noisyFeedback: It's quite noisy here. Results may be less accurate.
  tooShortFeedback: That was too short. Hold the key a little longer while you speak.
  noSpeechFeedback: We couldn't hear you. Try again closer to the microphone.
  noDifferenceFeedback: We couldn't hear a difference. Try again closer to the microphone.
  quietMicFeedback: We can barely hear you. Raise Mic volume or move closer to the
    microphone, then try again.
  loudNotLouderFeedback: That wasn't louder than your normal voice. Speak louder,
    or go Back and redo the normal step more quietly.
  normalTooLoudFeedback: Your normal voice is already too loud for this microphone
    to hear anything louder. Speak more quietly or lower Mic volume, then try again.
  holdToCaptureFormat: Hold {0}, say the phrase, then release. Next unlocks once
    it is captured.
  gainChangedFeedback: Mic volume changed - that recording was dropped. Try again.
  gainValueFormat: '{0}%'
  testFeedback: Looks good? Click Finish to save.
  disconnectedFeedback: Microphone disconnected. Choose a microphone to continue.
  noDeviceMessage: No microphone detected.
  unavailableMessage: The microphone is unavailable. Check that Windows allows this
    app to use it.
  skipLabelScene: Skip setup
  skipLabelOverlay: Cancel
  nextText: Next >
  finishText: Finish
  systemDefaultDeviceLabel: System default
  statusMessage: This setup appears only once. You can change it later in Control
    Panel.
